{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md && find .. -name AGENTS.md -print && git show --stat --oneline 66cde3e && git show --format=fuller --find-renames 66cde3e -- && git show --format=fuller --stat bcf4ac0 && git status --porcelain=v2\"","aggregated_output":"# T-104 — operator can retry a dead job\n\nState: In progress\nBranch: ticket/T-104-retry-dead-job\nRisk class: medium (touches the worker/queue lifecycle, but no external actions)\n\n## Description\n\nA job that fails 3 times goes to the dead-letter and stays there forever. Operators need a second chance after fixing the underlying cause: an explicit, auditable retry.\n\n- `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry` re-queues a **dead** job: it becomes pending again with a fresh attempt budget (3 more attempts), and the worker picks it up on its normal tick.\n- The job record keeps its history: total attempts accumulate across retries, and the record shows it was retried (planner freezes the representation, e.g. a retry count).\n- Retrying a job that is not dead is refused with a clear status code and no change (planner freezes which code).\n- Everything persists: a retry survives a kill/restart, and a re-queued job that keeps failing goes dead again after its 3 new attempts.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (planner freezes the exact contract)\n\n1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed (payload stops failing) completes and produces its proposed action as normal.\n2. A dead job, retried, still failing → dead again after exactly 3 new attempts, with cumulative attempts visible on the record.\n3. Retry of a non-dead job (pending or done) → refused with the frozen status code, record unchanged.\n4. Kill the server right after a retry is accepted; on restart the re-queued job is processed (crash recovery holds).\n\n## Planner note (lesson from T-102)\n\nBefore freezing the contract, enumerate every existing test that asserts exact response bodies this change would touch (`/health` queue counts, job objects in `/api/state`, the conformance suite's dead-letter test). If the contract necessarily breaks any of them, say so in the frozen contract and list the exact tests the test-author must amend *in the same test-authoring stage* — do not leave the collision for the builder to discover.\n\n## Frozen contract\n\n### `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry`\n\n`:id` is the job's `id` field exactly as it appears in `/api/state` (e.g. `job-e4`), matched against `state.jobs`, route regex `^\\/api\\/jobs\\/([^/]+)\\/retry$`. No request body is read or required.\n\n- Unknown `:id` → `404 { \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such job\" }`, no state change.\n- Job exists but `status !== \"dead\"` (i.e. `pending` or `done`) → `409 { \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"only dead jobs can be retried (status: <current-status>)\" }` — `<current-status>` is the literal current value of `job.status` (`\"pending\"` or `\"done\"`), record unchanged (no field, including `lastError`, is touched; no `persist()` call happens on this branch).\n- Job exists and `status === \"dead\"` → accepted:\n  - `job.status` → `\"pending\"`\n  - `job.attemptsSinceRetry` → reset to `0`\n  - `job.retries` → incremented by `1`\n  - `job.attempts` and `job.lastError` are **not** modified by the retry call itself (the next worker tick updates them exactly as it does today)\n  - state is persisted atomically before the response is sent\n  - Response: `200 { \"ok\": true, \"status\": \"pending\", \"retries\": <job.retries after increment> }`\n\n### `GET /api/state` — `jobs[]` shape (additive, present on every job from creation, not just retried ones)\n\nEvery job object gains two new keys, initialized at creation in `acceptEvent` alongside the existing `attempts: 0, lastError: null`:\n\n```json\n{ \"id\": \"job-e1\", \"eventId\": \"e1\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"attempts\": 0, \"lastError\": null, \"retries\": 0, \"attemptsSinceRetry\": 0 }\n```\n\n- `retries` (number): count of times `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry` has been accepted for this job. `0` until first retry, then increments by exactly `1` per accepted retry call. This is \"the record shows it was retried\" representation the ticket description asks the planner to freeze.\n- `attemptsSinceRetry` (number): attempts made since job creation, or since the most recent accepted retry, whichever is later. Incremented by `1` in the same worker tick that increments `attempts` (so it always equals `attempts` until the first retry, after which it runs ahead of `attempts` by the reset amount). This is the internal counter that drives the \"3 more attempts\" budget below — it is not itself a public promise beyond what AC1–AC4 require, but it is real state and will appear verbatim in `/api/state`, so the test-author may assert on it directly.\n- `attempts` is unchanged in meaning: **cumulative total attempts across the job's entire lifetime, including all retries** — never reset. This is the \"cumulative attempts visible on the record\" the ticket asks for.\n\n### Worker/dead-letter logic change (in `processJob`)\n\nToday: `if (job.attempts <= failTimes) { ...; if (job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \"dead\"; }`.\n\nNew: increment both `job.attempts` and `job.attemptsSinceRetry` on every attempt; the dead-letter check moves from `job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS` to `job.attemptsSinceRetry >= MAX_ATTEMPTS` (`MAX_ATTEMPTS` stays `3`, unchanged, reused as-is). The failure-vs-success check itself (`job.attempts <= failTimes`) stays keyed on cumulative `attempts`, not the reset counter — this is what makes \"payload stops failing\" (AC1) fall out for free: once cumulative `attempts` exceeds the event's fixed `failTimes`, every future attempt (retried or not) succeeds, without any payload mutation. For a job never retried, `attemptsSinceRetry === attempts` at all times, so pre-existing dead-lettering behavior (dead at exactly 3 cumulative attempts) is bit-for-bit unchanged.\n\n`workerTick` itself is unchanged: it still picks the first `status === \"pending\"` job in array order per tick, which already covers \"the worker picks it up on its normal tick\" for a re-queued job.\n\nIf this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\n\n## Existing test audit (planner note lesson from T-102)\n\nEvery test file in `conformance/app/tests/` (`conformance.test.js`, `health.test.js`, `health-approvals.test.js`, `reject-reason.test.js`) was read in full and grepped for `deepStrictEqual` / exact `JSON.stringify`/text-body matches, to find anything an added `retries` / `attemptsSinceRetry` job field, or a changed dead-letter trigger, could break:\n\n- `tests/health.test.js` (2 `assert.deepStrictEqual` on `GET /health`) and `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (3 exact `assertHealth` text matches) assert only the aggregate `{ ok, queue: {pending,done,dead}, approvals: {...} }` shape. `/health` counts jobs by `status` bucket only (`pending`/`done`/`dead`) and never serializes a job object; this ticket introduces no new `status` value (retried jobs return to the existing `\"pending\"` status) and adds no new top-level `/health` field. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- `tests/conformance.test.js` tests `\"3. transient failure...\"` and `\"4. permanent failure...\"` assert individual fields (`job.status`, `job.attempts`, `job.lastError` via `assert.strictEqual`/`assert.match`), never a full-object `deepStrictEqual` on a job. Both tests exercise jobs that are never retried, so `attemptsSinceRetry === attempts` throughout and the dead-letter trigger point (3 cumulative attempts) is unchanged for them. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- `tests/reject-reason.test.js` builds exact expected **approval** objects (`expectedApproval`) via `deepStrictEqual`, never touches `jobs[]`. Retry has no effect on approvals. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- No test file anywhere does `assert.deepStrictEqual` (or an exact `JSON.stringify`/full-body match) against an individual job object or against the full `jobs[]` array in `/api/state`.\n\n**Conclusion: zero existing tests require amendment.** `tests/retry-dead.test.js` is a purely additive new file; the test-author does not need to touch any pre-existing test file for this ticket.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- App lives in `conformance/app/` (zero-dependency Node 18+; see `conformance/SPEC.md`).\n- Tests go in `conformance/app/tests/` — new file `tests/retry-dead.test.js`, same style as the existing suites (node:test, spawn the real server on its own port with a temp DATA_DIR).\n- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/retry-dead.test.js`.\n\n## Log\n\n- 2026-07-12: ticket created by the operator; State → Ready. Second ticket of the loop trial; starts only after T-103 reaches AWAIT-OPERATOR or Done.\n- 2026-07-12: planner froze the `POST /api/jobs/:id/retry` contract (404 unknown job / 409 non-dead job / 200 accepted-with-`retries`-count) and the additive `retries` + `attemptsSinceRetry` job fields, including the dead-letter trigger moving from cumulative `attempts` to `attemptsSinceRetry`; audited all four existing test files (`conformance.test.js`, `health.test.js`, `health-approvals.test.js`, `reject-reason.test.js`) for exact-body collisions and found none — no pre-existing test needs amendment, `tests/retry-dead.test.js` is purely additive; branch `ticket/T-104-retry-dead-job` created off `main`, worktree at `~/Projects/sf-worktrees/T-104`; State → In progress.\n- 2026-07-12: planner (Claude Code) completed the frozen contract and exact-body audit at `e08f203`; zero existing tests require amendment; ledger cost $1.0210898.\n- 2026-07-12: test author added `tests/retry-dead.test.js` with one acceptance test each for: retry-to-success and normal proposed action creation; exactly three fresh failed attempts with cumulative attempt history; immutable `409` refusal for both pending and done jobs; and persisted retry processing after `SIGKILL` + restart. The suite also covers the exact frozen unknown-job `404` response. All four criteria were expressible as tests; no demo-check-only items.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) committed five frozen-contract checks at `b1d9ddf`; all five fail for the expected missing retry route/response behavior while all 20 existing tests pass; no product code or pre-existing tests changed; ledger cost $0.4673.\n- 2026-07-12: builder (Claude Code) implemented the frozen retry route, additive counters, and reset dead-letter budget in `conformance/app/server.js` at `aefdef1` without touching tests; full suite passes 25/25; ledger cost $0.5076823.\n- 2026-07-12 23:10:53: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The accepted-retry transition is not inspected before the worker advances. An implementation that incorrectly clears `lastError` during the retry would pass all 25 tests. Add a controlled-worker assertion immediately after the `200` response verifying persisted state is `pending`, `attempts` and `lastError` are unchanged, `attemptsSinceRetry` is `0`, and `retries` is `1`. The frozen rule that `retries` increments by exactly one per accepted retry is only tested for the first retry. Add a second dead → retry cycle and assert the response and job record report `retries: 2` while preserving cumulative attempts and resetting only the fresh-attempt counter. Commit order and test immutability are correct. The pre-builder state reproduces 20 existing passes and 5 intended failures; the current full suite independently passes 25/25. The implementation otherwise matches the frozen contract and conventions. Cost $0.2527.\n- 2026-07-12: test author addressed reviewer round 1 in `tests/retry-dead.test.js`: AC1 now restarts with a controlled long worker interval and verifies the persisted immediate accepted-retry transition preserves `attempts: 3` and `lastError` while setting `pending`, `retries: 1`, and `attemptsSinceRetry: 0`; AC2 now covers a second complete dead → retry → dead cycle, asserting the accepted response/record report `retries: 2`, cumulative attempts remain `6` at retry and reach `9` after exactly three fresh failures, and only `attemptsSinceRetry` resets. All criteria remain expressible as automated tests; no demo-check-only items.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) addressed reviewer round 1 at `66cde3e`; targeted suite passes 5/5 and full suite passes 25/25; only the acceptance tests and ticket log changed; ledger cost $0.3445.\n66cde3e T-104: cover immediate and repeated retry transitions\n conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md     |   1 +\n 2 files changed, 120 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\ncommit 66cde3e524f17a4ad1b0463652be94e7bb933240\nAuthor:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nAuthorDate: Sun Jul 12 23:13:59 2026 -0600\nCommit:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nCommitDate: Sun Jul 12 23:13:59 2026 -0600\n\n    T-104: cover immediate and repeated retry transitions\n\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js b/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\nindex f7d7737..e72f853 100644\n--- a/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\n+++ b/conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\n@@ -80,7 +80,13 @@ async function waitForJob(base, jobId, predicate, tries = 100) {\n }\n \n test(\"1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed completes and produces its proposed action as normal\", async () => {\n-  await withServer(4751, async ({ base }) => {\n+  const port = 4751;\n+  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n+  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-retry-transition-test-\"));\n+  let proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 50);\n+\n+  try {\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n     const eventId = \"retry-then-complete\";\n     const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n     await postEvent(base, eventId, {\n@@ -89,7 +95,25 @@ test(\"1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed compl\n       subject: \"Recovered action\",\n       body: \"The retry completed.\",\n     });\n-    await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\");\n+    const { job: deadJob } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, job => job.status === \"dead\");\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        attempts: deadJob.attempts,\n+        lastError: deadJob.lastError,\n+        retries: deadJob.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: deadJob.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      {\n+        attempts: 3,\n+        lastError: \"simulated failure on attempt 3\",\n+        retries: 0,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: 3,\n+      },\n+    );\n+\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 60_000);\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n \n     const response = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n     assert.strictEqual(response.status, 200);\n@@ -99,6 +123,30 @@ test(\"1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed compl\n       retries: 1,\n     });\n \n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 60_000);\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n+    const persistedRetry = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        status: persistedRetry.status,\n+        attempts: persistedRetry.attempts,\n+        lastError: persistedRetry.lastError,\n+        retries: persistedRetry.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: persistedRetry.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      {\n+        status: \"pending\",\n+        attempts: 3,\n+        lastError: \"simulated failure on attempt 3\",\n+        retries: 1,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: 0,\n+      },\n+    );\n+\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 50);\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n     const { job, state } = await waitForJob(base, jobId, item => item.status === \"done\");\n     assert.deepStrictEqual(\n       {\n@@ -124,11 +172,20 @@ test(\"1. A dead job, retried → pending again; a job whose cause is fixed compl\n         body: \"The retry completed.\",\n       },\n     );\n-  });\n+  } finally {\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+  }\n });\n \n test(\"2. A dead job, retried, still failing → dead again after exactly 3 new attempts, with cumulative attempts visible on the record\", async () => {\n-  await withServer(4752, async ({ base }) => {\n+  const port = 4752;\n+  const base = `http://localhost:${port}`;\n+  const dataDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"relay-second-retry-test-\"));\n+  let proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 50);\n+\n+  try {\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n     const eventId = \"retry-still-failing\";\n     const jobId = `job-${eventId}`;\n     await postEvent(base, eventId, { failTimes: 99 });\n@@ -163,7 +220,64 @@ test(\"2. A dead job, retried, still failing → dead again after exactly 3 new a\n         attemptsSinceRetry: 3,\n       },\n     );\n-  });\n+\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 60_000);\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n+    const secondResponse = await retryJob(base, jobId);\n+    assert.strictEqual(secondResponse.status, 200);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(await secondResponse.json(), {\n+      ok: true,\n+      status: \"pending\",\n+      retries: 2,\n+    });\n+\n+    const secondRetry = (await getState(base)).jobs.find(item => item.id === jobId);\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        status: secondRetry.status,\n+        attempts: secondRetry.attempts,\n+        lastError: secondRetry.lastError,\n+        retries: secondRetry.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: secondRetry.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      {\n+        status: \"pending\",\n+        attempts: 6,\n+        lastError: \"simulated failure on attempt 6\",\n+        retries: 2,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: 0,\n+      },\n+    );\n+\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    proc = startServer(port, dataDir, 50);\n+    await waitForHealth(base);\n+    const { job: twiceDeadJob } = await waitForJob(\n+      base,\n+      jobId,\n+      item => item.status === \"dead\" && item.retries === 2,\n+    );\n+    assert.deepStrictEqual(\n+      {\n+        status: twiceDeadJob.status,\n+        attempts: twiceDeadJob.attempts,\n+        lastError: twiceDeadJob.lastError,\n+        retries: twiceDeadJob.retries,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: twiceDeadJob.attemptsSinceRetry,\n+      },\n+      {\n+        status: \"dead\",\n+        attempts: 9,\n+        lastError: \"simulated failure on attempt 9\",\n+        retries: 2,\n+        attemptsSinceRetry: 3,\n+      },\n+    );\n+  } finally {\n+    await stopServer(proc);\n+    fs.rmSync(dataDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n+  }\n });\n \n test(\"3. Retry of a non-dead job (pending or done) → refused with 409, record unchanged\", async () => {\ndiff --git a/conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md b/conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md\nindex ccfc9da..34c004d 100644\n--- a/conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md\n+++ b/conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md\n@@ -88,3 +88,4 @@ Every test file in `conformance/app/tests/` (`conformance.test.js`, `health.test\n - 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) committed five frozen-contract checks at `b1d9ddf`; all five fail for the expected missing retry route/response behavior while all 20 existing tests pass; no product code or pre-existing tests changed; ledger cost $0.4673.\n - 2026-07-12: builder (Claude Code) implemented the frozen retry route, additive counters, and reset dead-letter budget in `conformance/app/server.js` at `aefdef1` without touching tests; full suite passes 25/25; ledger cost $0.5076823.\n - 2026-07-12 23:10:53: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The accepted-retry transition is not inspected before the worker advances. An implementation that incorrectly clears `lastError` during the retry would pass all 25 tests. Add a controlled-worker assertion immediately after the `200` response verifying persisted state is `pending`, `attempts` and `lastError` are unchanged, `attemptsSinceRetry` is `0`, and `retries` is `1`. The frozen rule that `retries` increments by exactly one per accepted retry is only tested for the first retry. Add a second dead → retry cycle and assert the response and job record report `retries: 2` while preserving cumulative attempts and resetting only the fresh-attempt counter. Commit order and test immutability are correct. The pre-builder state reproduces 20 existing passes and 5 intended failures; the current full suite independently passes 25/25. The implementation otherwise matches the frozen contract and conventions. Cost $0.2527.\n+- 2026-07-12: test author addressed reviewer round 1 in `tests/retry-dead.test.js`: AC1 now restarts with a controlled long worker interval and verifies the persisted immediate accepted-retry transition preserves `attempts: 3` and `lastError` while setting `pending`, `retries: 1`, and `attemptsSinceRetry: 0`; AC2 now covers a second complete dead → retry → dead cycle, asserting the accepted response/record report `retries: 2`, cumulative attempts remain `6` at retry and reach `9` after exactly three fresh failures, and only `attemptsSinceRetry` resets. All criteria remain expressible as automated tests; no demo-check-only items.\ncommit bcf4ac0a6bb05bfbdd555537f2714d2465442cba\nAuthor:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nAuthorDate: Sun Jul 12 23:14:46 2026 -0600\nCommit:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nCommitDate: Sun Jul 12 23:14:46 2026 -0600\n\n    T-104: log reviewer fix tests\n\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md | 1 +\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n? conformance/factory/runs/1783918994-98019.out\n? conformance/factory/runs/1783919207-99006.out\n? conformance/factory/runs/1783919328-99557.out\n? conformance/factory/runs/1783919498-394.out\n? conformance/factory/runs/1783919699-1499.out\n? conformance/factory/runs/1783919699-1499.pid\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
