{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '240,520p' conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js && git log --reverse --format='%h %s' main..HEAD && for c in e08f203 b1d9ddf b247ca7 aefdef1 0400111 16fe34c 66cde3e bcf4ac0; do git show --format='%h %s' --name-only \\\"\"'$c\" | sed '\"'/\"'^$/d'\"'; done && git diff --name-status main..HEAD && git diff --stat main..HEAD && git diff b1d9ddf\"'^:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js b1d9ddf:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js -- >/dev/null 2>&1; printf '\"'original-test-blob=%s\\\\nbuilder-parent-test-blob=%s\\\\nbuilder-test-blob=%s\\\\nround1-test-blob=%s\\\\nround2-test-blob=%s\\\\nhead-test-blob=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$(git rev-parse b1d9ddf:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js)\" \"$(git rev-parse aefdef1''^:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js)\" \"$(git rev-parse aefdef1:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js)\" \"$(git rev-parse 16fe34c:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js)\" \"$(git rev-parse 66cde3e:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js)\" \"$(git rev-parse HEAD:conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js)\" && rg -n \"node --test|immutability|commit order|test-immutability\" conformance scripts .github -g '\"'*.sh' -g '*.yml' -g '*.yaml' -g '*.md' -g 'package.json' | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"bcf4ac0 T-104: log reviewer fix tests\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md\nM\tconformance/app/server.js\nA\tconformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js\nM\tconformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md\n conformance/app/server.js                |  23 +-\n conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js | 373 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md     |  61 ++++-\n 3 files changed, 454 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\noriginal-test-blob=f7d7737d13eed16c86d32a69e1dc84e18d468034\nbuilder-parent-test-blob=f7d7737d13eed16c86d32a69e1dc84e18d468034\nbuilder-test-blob=f7d7737d13eed16c86d32a69e1dc84e18d468034\nround1-test-blob=f7d7737d13eed16c86d32a69e1dc84e18d468034\nround2-test-blob=e72f853bd2b686a4170f339f1086a3bb960a5834\nhead-test-blob=e72f853bd2b686a4170f339f1086a3bb960a5834\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:23:  test-immutability:\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:30:        run: bash ci/test-immutability-check.sh\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:59:- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/health-approvals.test.js`.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:76:- 2026-07-12 21:19:36: reviewer round 2: APPROVE — round 1 was addressed exactly, commit order and test-immutability discipline hold, implementation matches the frozen contract, and the full suite passes 15/15; cost $0.1258.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:78:- 2026-07-12: Javier approved PR #2 and it was squash-merged to main as `1a62289`; the operator rebased the ticket branch before merge to satisfy the commit-order gate, and the test-immutability gate now exempts factory bookkeeping paths; State → Done.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md:33:- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/health.test.js`.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md:40:- 2026-07-12: reviewer (codex) round 1 REQUEST CHANGES — tests didn't assert HTTP 200 and a hard-coded pending:0 would pass. Test-author round 2 added both (a2f5a72, rebased before implementation; immutability gate green). Reviewer round 2: APPROVE.\nconformance/app/package.json:8:    \"test\": \"node --test tests/*.test.js\"\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:80:- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/retry-dead.test.js`.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:90:- 2026-07-12 23:10:53: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The accepted-retry transition is not inspected before the worker advances. An implementation that incorrectly clears `lastError` during the retry would pass all 25 tests. Add a controlled-worker assertion immediately after the `200` response verifying persisted state is `pending`, `attempts` and `lastError` are unchanged, `attemptsSinceRetry` is `0`, and `retries` is `1`. The frozen rule that `retries` increments by exactly one per accepted retry is only tested for the first retry. Add a second dead → retry cycle and assert the response and job record report `retries: 2` while preserving cumulative attempts and resetting only the fresh-attempt counter. Commit order and test immutability are correct. The pre-builder state reproduces 20 existing passes and 5 intended failures; the current full suite independently passes 25/25. The implementation otherwise matches the frozen contract and conventions. Cost $0.2527.\nconformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:15:| Test-immutability gate | passes on a clean builder branch; fails (exit 1) when a builder commit touches a test file |\nconformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:23:3. **`node --test <dir>` misbehaved**; the test script pins the explicit file. Trivial, but exactly the class of scaffold bug the walking skeleton exists to catch.\nconformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:25:5. **Ticket branches must merge, not delete.** During the immutability demo the ticket branch was deleted unmerged and the shakedown's own adapter fixes were nearly lost (recovered via reflog). The ticket-flow doc's rule — one branch, one PR, merged via approval — exists for a reason; the drill violated it and paid.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:55:node --test tests/*.js\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:86:7. **Reviewer round 2: APPROVE** — round 1 addressed exactly, commit order and test-immutability discipline hold, implementation matches the frozen contract, full suite passes.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-101-bundle.md:49:All gates green: health tests 4/4, full conformance suite 8/8, immutability gate green. Reviewer verdict (round 2): APPROVE.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:65:- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/reject-reason.test.js`.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:84:- 2026-07-12 22:36:03: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The frozen unknown-ID contract is untested. The builder changed reject-response serialization to remove the internal `code` field, but tests only verify exact `409` bodies. An implementation that fixes `409` while returning the wrong `404` body would pass all 19 tests. Add a test asserting an unknown approval returns HTTP `404` with exactly `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such approval\" }`. Criteria 1–4 are otherwise adequately tested. Commit order and test immutability are correct, and the full suite independently passes 19/19. Cost $0.2206.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:86:- 2026-07-12 22:40:20: reviewer round 2: APPROVE — The added test correctly asserts both HTTP `404` and the exact frozen body `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such approval\" }`; it would catch the prior leaked `code` field. Criteria 1–4 remain adequately tested. The implementation matches the frozen contract without scope creep, original acceptance tests were unchanged by the builder, the requested regression test is an additive later commit, commit order is correct, and the independently rerun full suite passes 20/20. Cost $0.1490.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:71:node --test tests/*.js\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:101:- **Round 2 — APPROVE**: new test correctly catches the prior leaked-`code`-field risk; all four criteria adequately tested; implementation matches the frozen contract with no scope creep; original acceptance tests untouched by the builder; commit order correct; full suite independently rerun 20/20.\nconformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:126:**Internal change — low risk**, per the evidence rubric. No `external` label: rejecting a proposal cannot trigger a send — the outbox is untouched by this ticket, and this only adds metadata (`reason`) to an existing record. No schema migration is involved; the `reason` field is additive and only appears on already-rejected approvals. Worst plausible failure is a wrong or leaked `reason` value on a rejected approval, which the acceptance tests guard against with exact `deepStrictEqual` checks on the full approval object, including the non-pending/immutability and restart-persistence paths.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' ci/test-immutability-check.sh && sed -n '1,120p' .github/workflows/ci.yml && sed -n '1,220p' conformance/factory/ENVELOPE.md && git diff main..HEAD -- conformance/app/server.js && git show --format=fuller --stat aefdef1 && git show --format= --name-status aefdef1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' ci/test-immutability-check.sh && sed -n '1,120p' .github/workflows/ci.yml && sed -n '1,220p' conformance/factory/ENVELOPE.md && git diff main..HEAD -- conformance/app/server.js && git show --format=fuller --stat aefdef1 && git show --format= --name-status aefdef1\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# test-immutability-check.sh — CI gate enforcing two mechanical rules that\n# need no trusted commit identity (identity markers are agent-controlled and\n# were a self-exemption bypass in v1 of this script):\n#\n#   Rule 1 — separation: a commit either touches only test paths (a \"test\n#   commit\") or touches no test paths (an \"implementation commit\"). A commit\n#   mixing both fails: that is a builder bundling test edits with code.\n#\n#   Rule 2 — order: every test commit must precede every implementation\n#   commit on the branch. Tests are authored first and frozen; any test\n#   change after implementation started fails the gate.\n#\n# A builder pushing a late test-only commit is caught by Rule 2. The reviewer\n# additionally verifies session/PR provenance of the test commits.\n#\n# Factory bookkeeping (ticket logs, ledgers) is neither test nor\n# implementation: dispatcher log commits interleave with every stage and must\n# not trip the ordering rule. EXEMPT_PATHS names those pathspecs; files under\n# them are ignored entirely by both rules.\n#\n# Env: BASE_REF (default origin/main), TEST_PATHS (space-separated pathspecs,\n# default \"tests/\"), EXEMPT_PATHS (default \"factory/ conformance/factory/\").\n# Wire as a required GitHub Actions status on every PR.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nBASE_REF=\"${BASE_REF:-origin/main}\"\nTEST_PATHS=\"${TEST_PATHS:-tests/}\"\nEXEMPT_PATHS=\"${EXEMPT_PATHS:-factory/ conformance/factory/}\"\nFAIL=0\nSEEN_IMPL=0\n\nis_exempt() { # path -> 0 if under any exempt prefix\n  local f=\"$1\" p\n  for p in $EXEMPT_PATHS; do\n    [[ \"$f\" == \"$p\"* ]] && return 0\n  done\n  return 1\n}\n\n# oldest → newest, so ordering can be checked in one pass\nfor COMMIT in $(git rev-list --reverse \"$BASE_REF\"..HEAD); do\n  MSG=\"$(git log -1 --format=%s \"$COMMIT\")\"\n  ALL_FILES=\"\"\n  while IFS= read -r F; do\n    [[ -z \"$F\" ]] && continue\n    is_exempt \"$F\" || ALL_FILES+=\"$F\"$'\\n'\n  done < <(git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-only -r \"$COMMIT\")\n  ALL_FILES=\"${ALL_FILES%$'\\n'}\"\n  # shellcheck disable=SC2086\n  TEST_FILES=\"$(git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-only -r \"$COMMIT\" -- $TEST_PATHS)\"\n  NONTEST_FILES=\"$(comm -23 <(sort <<<\"$ALL_FILES\") <(sort <<<\"$TEST_FILES\") | sed '/^$/d')\"\n\n  if [[ -n \"$TEST_FILES\" && -n \"$NONTEST_FILES\" ]]; then\n    echo \"FAIL (rule 1, separation): commit $COMMIT ('$MSG') mixes test and non-test changes:\" >&2\n    echo \"$TEST_FILES\" | sed 's/^/  test: /' >&2\n    echo \"$NONTEST_FILES\" | sed 's/^/  impl: /' >&2\n    FAIL=1\n  elif [[ -n \"$TEST_FILES\" ]]; then\n    if [[ $SEEN_IMPL -eq 1 ]]; then\n      echo \"FAIL (rule 2, order): test commit $COMMIT ('$MSG') comes after implementation started — tests are frozen once building begins:\" >&2\n      echo \"$TEST_FILES\" | sed 's/^/  test: /' >&2\n      FAIL=1\n    fi\n  elif [[ -n \"$NONTEST_FILES\" ]]; then\n    SEEN_IMPL=1\n  fi\ndone\n\nif [[ $FAIL -eq 0 ]]; then\n  echo \"test immutability holds: test commits are pure and all precede implementation ($TEST_PATHS)\"\nfi\nexit $FAIL\n# Live CI for this repo, instantiated from ci/github-actions-ci.template.yml.\n# The \"product\" here is the Relay conformance app; when the kit is\n# instantiated for a real product, that repo gets its own copy.\nname: ci\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  ci:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n      - name: tests\n        run: npm test\n        working-directory: conformance/app\n\n  test-immutability:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0   # the check walks every commit on the branch\n      - name: builder commits must not touch tests\n        run: bash ci/test-immutability-check.sh\n        env:\n          BASE_REF: origin/${{ github.base_ref || 'main' }}\n          TEST_PATHS: conformance/app/tests/\n# Operating envelope — Relay (conformance shakedown)\n\nFilled from the kit template with deliberately tiny limits: the shakedown's job is to hit them.\n\n| Limit | Value | Enforced by |\n|---|---|---|\n| Per-ticket budget (USD) | $0.50 | run wrapper / `--max-budget-usd` |\n| Per-run max turns | 15 | logged (Claude Code 2.1.207 dropped `--max-turns`; budget is the hard stop) |\n| Per-run wall-clock cap | 5 min | run wrapper timeout |\n| Daily factory cap (USD) | $2.00 | run wrapper ledger check |\n\nRetries/escalation: 2 reviewer rounds; 2 builder attempts; then Blocked-Escalated. External actions: Relay's allowlist is `test@example.com` only — production mode does not exist in this product by design.\n\nExit thresholds don't apply (this is the kit's own test, not a product pilot).\ndiff --git a/conformance/app/server.js b/conformance/app/server.js\nindex ef04468..ffc00cd 100644\n--- a/conformance/app/server.js\n+++ b/conformance/app/server.js\n@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@ function acceptEvent(evt) {\n     status: \"pending\", // pending | done | dead\n     attempts: 0,\n     lastError: null,\n+    retries: 0,\n+    attemptsSinceRetry: 0,\n   });\n   persist();\n   return { ok: true, duplicate: false, eventId: evt.id };\n@@ -52,12 +54,13 @@ function acceptEvent(evt) {\n function processJob(job) {\n   const evt = state.events.find(e => e.id === job.eventId);\n   job.attempts += 1;\n+  job.attemptsSinceRetry += 1;\n   // Simulated transient/permanent failure: payload.failTimes = number of\n   // attempts that must fail before success (99 = effectively permanent).\n   const failTimes = Number(evt?.payload?.failTimes || 0);\n   if (job.attempts <= failTimes) {\n     job.lastError = `simulated failure on attempt ${job.attempts}`;\n-    if (job.attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \"dead\";\n+    if (job.attemptsSinceRetry >= MAX_ATTEMPTS) job.status = \"dead\";\n     persist();\n     return;\n   }\n@@ -109,6 +112,19 @@ function reject(id, body) {\n   return { ok: true, status: \"rejected\", reason };\n }\n \n+function retryJob(id) {\n+  const job = state.jobs.find(j => j.id === id);\n+  if (!job) return { ok: false, code: 404, error: \"no such job\" };\n+  if (job.status !== \"dead\") {\n+    return { ok: false, code: 409, error: `only dead jobs can be retried (status: ${job.status})` };\n+  }\n+  job.status = \"pending\";\n+  job.attemptsSinceRetry = 0;\n+  job.retries += 1;\n+  persist();\n+  return { ok: true, code: 200, status: \"pending\", retries: job.retries };\n+}\n+\n // ---------- http ----------\n function json(res, code, obj) {\n   res.writeHead(code, { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" });\n@@ -166,6 +182,11 @@ const server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\n       const { code, ...result } = reject(mReject[1], body);\n       return json(res, result.ok ? 200 : code, result);\n     }\n+    const mRetry = url.pathname.match(/^\\/api\\/jobs\\/([^/]+)\\/retry$/);\n+    if (req.method === \"POST\" && mRetry) {\n+      const { code, ...result } = retryJob(mRetry[1]);\n+      return json(res, code, result);\n+    }\n     json(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n   } catch (e) {\n     json(res, 400, { error: String(e.message || e) });\ncommit aefdef16bf61fb34854d21fa3664c8efa343a321\nAuthor:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nAuthorDate: Sun Jul 12 23:07:57 2026 -0600\nCommit:     hermes-dispatcher <hermes-dispatcher@nysa-company.local>\nCommitDate: Sun Jul 12 23:07:57 2026 -0600\n\n    T-104: implement retry-dead-job route and dead-letter budget reset\n    \n    Adds POST /api/jobs/:id/retry per the frozen contract: 404 unknown job,\n    409 non-dead job (status unchanged), 200 accepted (pending + retries++).\n    Jobs gain retries/attemptsSinceRetry fields; dead-letter trigger moves\n    from cumulative attempts to attemptsSinceRetry so a retry grants a fresh\n    3-attempt budget while attempts keeps accumulating across the job's\n    lifetime.\n\n conformance/app/server.js | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\nM\tconformance/app/server.js\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
